    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\cos^{3}{\\theta} + \\cos{\\theta}\\sin^{2}{\\theta}$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n\\sin^{2}{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}+\\cos^{3}{\\theta}=\\cos{\\theta}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\theta}+\\cos^{2}{\\theta})\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^{2}{\\theta}+\\cos^{2}{\\theta}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cos{\\theta}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\theta}+\\cos^{2}{\\theta}) & =\\cos{\\theta}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\cos{\\theta}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sin^{2}{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}+\\cos^{3}{\\theta}=\\cos{\\theta}.\n$$",
