      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we factor $\\sin{x}\\cos{x}$ from the expression:\n\n$$\n\\sin{x}\\cos^{3}{x}+\\sin^{3}{x}\\cos{x}=\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\\cdot (\\cos^{2}{x}+\\sin^{2}{x})\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\cos^{2}{x}+\\sin^{2}{x}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\\cdot (\\sin^{2}{x}+\\cos^{2}{x}) & =\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sin{x}\\cos^{3}{x}+\\sin^{3}{x}\\cos{x}=\\sin{x}\\cos{x}.\n$$",
